(7265679, 1130390, 163430, '<td valign="top">I like the pure joy that radiates from the scene.<br/>Not very fond of the old photo style of processing, though, but that just me.</td>', 'I like the pure joy that radiates from the scene.Not very fond of the old photo style of processing, though, but that just me.', '2014-09-24 06:22:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(7265720, 1130474, 61396, '<td valign="top">that''s an ursula</td>', 'that''s an ursula', '2014-09-24 10:12:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(7265731, 1130021, 103142, '<td valign="top">I wish you hadn''t added aka dinner prep. The title was awesome. :)<br/> <br/>I''m giving this a 9 now, because I think I''d give it something lower in the week if it''s impact fades. But I love the initial impact.<br/> <br/>I find it difficult to shoot multiple objects and have them blend together into a cohesive whole. This is an excellent example of something that doesn''t necessarily blend, but moves your eye through a picture without losing interest. Many times if your eye moves around, it''s because it''s distracted. There are few pictures that actually make my eye really roam, search, and want to keep searching more. I probably would have done the shot straight on to the sink, which would have been so incredibly wrong. The wonky angle gives this a tension and the water gives it movement. <br/> <br/>I think this is the longest comment I''ve made in quite awhile, but I''m just surprised how interesting I find this, and how it''s staying with me. Nice choices all the way around. -9-</td>', 'I wish you hadn''t added aka dinner prep. The title was awesome. :) I''m giving this a 9 now, because I think I''d give it something lower in the week if it''s impact fades. But I love the initial impact. I find it difficult to shoot multiple objects and have them blend together into a cohesive whole. This is an excellent example of something that doesn''t necessarily blend, but moves your eye through a picture without losing interest. Many times if your eye moves around, it''s because it''s distracted. There are few pictures that actually make my eye really roam, search, and want to keep searching more. I probably would have done the shot straight on to the sink, which would have been so incredibly wrong. The wonky angle gives this a tension and the water gives it movement.  I think this is the longest comment I''ve made in quite awhile, but I''m just surprised how interesting I find this, and how it''s staying with me. Nice choices all the way around. -9-', '2014-09-24 10:44:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(7265733, 1130436, 177322, '<td valign="top">The high-key lighting makes this an especially refreshing interpretation of the challenge.  Nicely executed.</td>', 'The high-key lighting makes this an especially refreshing interpretation of the challenge.  Nicely executed.', '2014-09-24 10:46:56.000000', NULL, 1),
