(7269728, 1130378, 124982, '<td valign="top">Hi Janine, greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>With a placing of 14 out of 89, it''s clear this image resonated well with the viewer, especially considering you averaged more 7''s than 5''s. <br/> <br/>For the positives, I really like the centered composition and the phenomenal detail. The reflection in the water is particularly beautiful too. However, where it falls short, in my view, is the processing. While I understand that HDR and HDR-like effects are very popular with the DPC crowd, I feel it is often over-done, as is the case here. The tonemapping has been pushed a little too far for me, to such a degree that the subject no longer appears natural. The image needs more shadows and contrast to make it believable. The other things with the processing is that the area to the immediate right of the pier (ie. water and sky) appear darker and "browner" than the the main body. Either this is a masking issue, or an issue with the processing, but the two parts of the image don''t look like they belong together. Lastly, I found that the whole image appears to be sloping badly to the left (I can tell you did straighten the horizon, but the angle of the incoming wave gives the tilted effect..not much you could do about that!).<br/> <br/>I know it appears I am being overly critical (which I probably am), but I do so in an effort to be as honest with my critique as possible and to let you know what I was feeling when I evaluated the image. <br/> <br/>If you have any questions/comments about my critique, please feel free to PM me!<br/> <br/>Kind regards,<br/>Garry</td>', 'Hi Janine, greetings from the Critique Club :) With a placing of 14 out of 89, it''s clear this image resonated well with the viewer, especially considering you averaged more 7''s than 5''s.  For the positives, I really like the centered composition and the phenomenal detail. The reflection in the water is particularly beautiful too. However, where it falls short, in my view, is the processing. While I understand that HDR and HDR-like effects are very popular with the DPC crowd, I feel it is often over-done, as is the case here. The tonemapping has been pushed a little too far for me, to such a degree that the subject no longer appears natural. The image needs more shadows and contrast to make it believable. The other things with the processing is that the area to the immediate right of the pier (ie. water and sky) appear darker and "browner" than the the main body. Either this is a masking issue, or an issue with the processing, but the two parts of the image don''t look like they belong together. Lastly, I found that the whole image appears to be sloping badly to the left (I can tell you did straighten the horizon, but the angle of the incoming wave gives the tilted effect..not much you could do about that!). I know it appears I am being overly critical (which I probably am), but I do so in an effort to be as honest with my critique as possible and to let you know what I was feeling when I evaluated the image.  If you have any questions/comments about my critique, please feel free to PM me! Kind regards,Garry', '2014-10-05 15:24:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(7269853, 1130331, 96311, '<td valign="top">Wow thanks for your kind words :-) i think the main thing for me is regularly going out with the camera and taking photos whenever possible. I had a day where i just decided to take off in the car and lose myself for a few hours, if i''d stayed home i wouldnt of taken this ! I do a regular trip every week with hesitant after work and we compete with each other, its fun but pushes you to try that little bit harder to improve ! I normaly have toast and coffee for breakfast if it helps ;-)<br/>Rob<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by chalice:</b></div><hr/><i> Congratulations on the Blue Ribbon.  It''s well-deserved.<br/> <br/>I just noticed your recent run of achievements:  Six consecutive challenges with HM or better and 10 out of the last 13 challenges with HM or a ribbon.  I''m not sure what you are eating for breakfast, but I need to eat some too.  Seriously, though, that''s an astounding achievement!  Congratulations. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Wow thanks for your kind words :-) i think the main thing for me is regularly going out with the camera and taking photos whenever possible. I had a day where i just decided to take off in the car and lose myself for a few hours, if i''d stayed home i wouldnt of taken this ! I do a regular trip every week with hesitant after work and we compete with each other, its fun but pushes you to try that little bit harder to improve ! I normaly have toast and coffee for breakfast if it helps ;-)Rob Originally posted by chalice: Congratulations on the Blue Ribbon.  It''s well-deserved. I just noticed your recent run of achievements:  Six consecutive challenges with HM or better and 10 out of the last 13 challenges with HM or a ribbon.  I''m not sure what you are eating for breakfast, but I need to eat some too.  Seriously, though, that''s an astounding achievement!  Congratulations. ', '2014-10-05 19:35:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(7269854, 1130213, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>I see a very surreal approach to this challenge in this image, which also makes me a little uneasy.  I don''t know why, yet.  <br/> <br/>Yes, this is a water challenge, and there is water splashed on the glass, and it does add interest to the photo; I like the composition.  I think, however, that the soft-focus effect and low light on your model makes her look a bit blueish and hence...well, either very ill or dead!  Hence the feeling of uneasiness, the slackness in her hand and half-closed/closed eyes just give too much a sense of remoteness from the viewer.<br/> <br/>I do hope this critique has been useful, feel free to PM me,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! I see a very surreal approach to this challenge in this image, which also makes me a little uneasy.  I don''t know why, yet.   Yes, this is a water challenge, and there is water splashed on the glass, and it does add interest to the photo; I like the composition.  I think, however, that the soft-focus effect and low light on your model makes her look a bit blueish and hence...well, either very ill or dead!  Hence the feeling of uneasiness, the slackness in her hand and half-closed/closed eyes just give too much a sense of remoteness from the viewer. I do hope this critique has been useful, feel free to PM me, Susan', '2014-10-05 19:47:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(7269855, 1130147, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Yay, I get to critique a fellow Canuck...but also a PB and an HM finish...no pressure ;-) And as also am very familiar with maples and tap some of mine for <i>sirop d''erable</i> each spring, I appreciate the backlit red maple leaves.<br/> <br/>Nice composition and lighting (though be careful, some may have thought this a tiny bit underexposed and voted accordingly). Lovely rich saturated colours, especially on the leaves, nice sharp detail on the droplets and the cool green/blue tones of the background which complement the scarlet perfectly...hard to pick holes in this one!<br/> <br/>Great work, continue to shoot and please continue to enter challenges!<br/> <br/>Hope this critique has been of help, feel free to PM me,<br/> <br/>Susan<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2014-10-05 18:59:21.</i></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Yay, I get to critique a fellow Canuck...but also a PB and an HM finish...no pressure ;-) And as also am very familiar with maples and tap some of mine for sirop d''erable each spring, I appreciate the backlit red maple leaves. Nice composition and lighting (though be careful, some may have thought this a tiny bit underexposed and voted accordingly). Lovely rich saturated colours, especially on the leaves, nice sharp detail on the droplets and the cool green/blue tones of the background which complement the scarlet perfectly...hard to pick holes in this one! Great work, continue to shoot and please continue to enter challenges! Hope this critique has been of help, feel free to PM me, Susan', '2014-10-05 19:56:16.000000', '2014-10-05 19:59:21.000000', 0),
(7270430, 1130458, 18505, '<td valign="top">Beautiful!!  Congratulations on your HM!!!</td>', 'Beautiful!!  Congratulations on your HM!!!', '2014-10-06 22:40:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(7273857, 1130117, 60173, '<td valign="top">Still dumbfounded that this got 15th. I really would have thought this had universal appeal.</td>', 'Still dumbfounded that this got 15th. I really would have thought this had universal appeal.', '2014-10-15 12:28:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(7424698, 1130377, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>First of all huge kudos to your model, what a trooper to put up with sitting in a waterfall and getting drenched. If this is for a model''s port, I''d book her! The concept is great but execution is a little weak. While your composition is ok with a good use of thirds, that cut-off toe of both boots just drives me nuts.  Don''t know if you just shot really tight to the subject and forgot to include the feet, or if she lost them in post, but the result is very amateurish.<br/> <br/>This pic has a lot of flaws that could have easily been fixed.  First, shooting more frames may have given you a shot where her eye isn''t blocked by water drops; your ISO looks a little high, I''m guessing you exposed for the water and not for her.  So there is a ton of bleachiness going on both in the water and on her skin.  Finally the overall image could use some saturation to pop the colours a little bit more.<br/> <br/>Hope this has been helpful,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! First of all huge kudos to your model, what a trooper to put up with sitting in a waterfall and getting drenched. If this is for a model''s port, I''d book her! The concept is great but execution is a little weak. While your composition is ok with a good use of thirds, that cut-off toe of both boots just drives me nuts.  Don''t know if you just shot really tight to the subject and forgot to include the feet, or if she lost them in post, but the result is very amateurish. This pic has a lot of flaws that could have easily been fixed.  First, shooting more frames may have given you a shot where her eye isn''t blocked by water drops; your ISO looks a little high, I''m guessing you exposed for the water and not for her.  So there is a ton of bleachiness going on both in the water and on her skin.  Finally the overall image could use some saturation to pop the colours a little bit more. Hope this has been helpful, Susan', '2015-12-29 20:26:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(7424703, 1130041, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Someone really meant it when they said they had a house on the water, didn''t they? :-) I love the tones here, the spectrum of blues is fantastic. Strong focal point, even though centred composition isn''t my favourite, but some like the symmetry as evinced in the comments.  I do agree that shooting with a smaller aperture would have given a much cleaner appearance here.  That and some saturation in post to pop the blues without going too heavy handed would have helped greatly.  <br/> <br/>Hope this helps<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Someone really meant it when they said they had a house on the water, didn''t they? :-) I love the tones here, the spectrum of blues is fantastic. Strong focal point, even though centred composition isn''t my favourite, but some like the symmetry as evinced in the comments.  I do agree that shooting with a smaller aperture would have given a much cleaner appearance here.  That and some saturation in post to pop the blues without going too heavy handed would have helped greatly.   Hope this helps Susan', '2015-12-29 20:31:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(7424896, 1130037, 86447, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Yeah, I''m sorry that your image has only just now come up for critique and sorry that you''re now gone after entering only this one image.<br/> <br/>I''d really enjoy seeing more of your images!  Please come back and enter again.<br/> <br/>This one is lovely.  The colors are stunning... and the capture is very well done.<br/> <br/>It scored well, but I think if she''d been throwing water over her instead of the scarf, it would have fit the challenge better and therefore scored higher.<br/> <br/>Regardless, this is an image to be proud of.<br/> <br/>I really enjoy it.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Yeah, I''m sorry that your image has only just now come up for critique and sorry that you''re now gone after entering only this one image. I''d really enjoy seeing more of your images!  Please come back and enter again. This one is lovely.  The colors are stunning... and the capture is very well done. It scored well, but I think if she''d been throwing water over her instead of the scarf, it would have fit the challenge better and therefore scored higher. Regardless, this is an image to be proud of. I really enjoy it. ', '2015-12-30 17:26:35.000000', NULL, 0);
